/*  Failures — `<type> or failure`, `return a failure …`, `or pass the failure off`, `but on failure`,
    `Try to: … In case of failure:`, `the message of the failure`, and reading a file, which can fail.

    ★ A value that may be a failure is `{ ok, value, failure }` — the failure the runtime's own
      `CufetFailure`, a message and a category that is NULL when none was given. Its kind is written
      `failure of <kind>`, `failure of void` for a call made for its effect.

    ★ INSIDE A `Try`, a call that can fail reads as its value: when it fails, the failure is kept and
      the program jumps to the handler — out of the middle of an expression, which gcc allows from a
      statement expression. The emitter's `kinds` map carries the `Try` a statement is in as `%try`,
      so a handler, a function and a block each see the right one.

    ⚠ `In case of exception` waits: it needs the runtime's own raising, a separate piece.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind fact to is-failable, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "failure of ".
    Done.

    /// What a failable kind holds when it is no failure.
    Bind text to failable-inner, given (the text kind):
        Return the characters from 12 to the end of kind.
    Done.

    Bind text to failable-c-name, given (the text kind):
        Define inner as cast failable-inner on (kind).
        If inner is "void", return "cfl_void".
        Return "cfl_{cast c-tag on (inner)}".
    Done.

    /// A failable's struct, and how one is made from a value, from a failure, or as done.
    Bind text to c-failable-helpers, given (the text kind):
        Define type-c as cast failable-c-name on (kind).
        Define inner as cast failable-inner on (kind).
        Define out as a chase.
        If inner is "void":
            Insert "typedef struct \{ int ok; CufetFailure failure; \} {type-c};\n" into out.
            Insert "static {type-c} {type-c}_done(void) \{ {type-c} o; memset(&o, 0, sizeof o); o.ok = 1; return o; \}\n" into out.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Insert "typedef struct \{ int ok; {cast c-type on (inner)} value; CufetFailure failure; \} {type-c};\n" into out.
            Insert "static {type-c} {type-c}_some({cast c-type on (inner)} v) \{ {type-c} o; memset(&o, 0, sizeof o); o.ok = 1; o.value = v; return o; \}\n" into out.
        Done.
        Insert "static {type-c} {type-c}_fail(CufetFailure f) \{ {type-c} o; memset(&o, 0, sizeof o); o.ok = 0; o.failure = f; return o; \}\n\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// Notes a failable type the program uses, after what it holds.
    Bind void to register-failable unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        If (the entry for kind in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for kind becomes true.
            Insert kind into one's union-order.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The kind of a written `<type> or failure`.
    Bind text or failure to failable-kind-of-type unto emitter, given (the node written):
        Define inner as "void".
        If (cast field-of on (written, 1))'s kind is not "VoidType":
            The inner becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If cast is-failable on (inner), return a failure (cast not-built on ("a failure of a {inner}")).
        Define kind as "failure of {inner}".
        Cast one's register-failable on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    /// A value going into a failable place: a failure as one, a value as a success.
    Bind text to c-into-failable unto emitter, given (the text value, the text source-kind, the text wanted):
        Define type-c as cast failable-c-name on (wanted).
        If source-kind is "failure", return "{type-c}_fail({value})".
        Return "{type-c}_some({cast one's c-coerce on (value, source-kind, cast failable-inner on (wanted))})".
    Done.

    /// The `Try` a statement is in — the label its failures go to — or "".
    Bind text to current-try unto emitter:
        Return the entry for "%try" in one's kinds but void is "".
    Done.

    /// The kind and C of an expression as it is, outside any `Try` — a failable left failable.
    Bind text or failure to raw-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kept as cast one's current-try.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes "".
        Define kind as cast one's kind-of on (expression) but on failure "".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes kept.
        If kind is "", return cast one's kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Return kind.
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to raw-c-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kept as cast one's current-try.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes "".
        Define written as cast one's c-of on (expression) but on failure "".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes kept.
        If written is "", return cast one's c-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Return written.
    Done.

    /// What a call that can fail reads as here: inside a `Try`, its value.
    Bind text to unwrapped-kind unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        If cast is-failable on (kind) and cast one's current-try is not "", return cast failable-inner on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    /// A call that can fail, as C: inside a `Try`, its value — or, when it fails, a jump to the handler.
    Bind text to c-unwrapped unto emitter, given (the text written, the text kind):
        Define label as cast one's current-try.
        If cast is-failable on (kind) is false or label is "", return written.
        Define taken as "(\{ {cast failable-c-name on (kind)} cf_r = {written}; if (!cf_r.ok) \{ cf_failure_{label} = cf_r.failure; goto cf_try_{label}; \}".
        If cast failable-inner on (kind) is "void", return "{taken} (void)0; \})".
        Return "{taken} cf_r.value; \})".
    Done.

    /// `<call> or pass the failure off` — its value, or the failure handed to this function's caller.
    Bind text or failure to c-pass-off unto emitter, given (the node held):
        Define kind as cast one's raw-kind-of on (held) or pass the failure off.
        Define written as cast one's raw-c-of on (held) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-failable on (kind) is false, return written.
        Define outer as the entry for "%return" in one's kinds but void is "".
        If cast is-failable on (outer) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("passing a failure off from where nothing can fail")).
        Define taken as "(\{ {cast failable-c-name on (kind)} cf_r = {written}; if (!cf_r.ok) return {cast failable-c-name on (outer)}_fail(cf_r.failure);".
        If cast failable-inner on (kind) is "void", return "{taken} (void)0; \})".
        Return "{taken} cf_r.value; \})".
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind fact to is-failure-expression, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "FailureLiteral" or kind is "FailurePropagate" or kind is "FailureFallback" or kind is "FileReadExpression".
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to failure-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "FailureLiteral", return "failure".
        If kind is "FileReadExpression":
            Define read-kind as "failure of text".
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is "AllLines", the read-kind becomes "failure of series of text".
            Otherwise if (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is not "All", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a file read of {(cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word}")).
            Cast one's register-failable on (read-kind).
            Return cast one's unwrapped-kind on (read-kind).
        Done.
        Define held as cast one's raw-kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-failable on (held) is false, return held.
        Return cast failable-inner on (held).
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to c-failure-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "FailureLiteral":
            Define said as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define tagged as "NULL".
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) is false:
                The tagged becomes cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Return "((CufetFailure)\{ {said}, {tagged} \})".
        Done.
        If kind is "FileReadExpression":
            Define path-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Define read-c as "".
            Define read-kind as "failure of text".
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is "AllLines":
                The read-kind becomes "failure of series of text".
                The read-c becomes "(\{ cfl_cser_text cf_fr; memset(&cf_fr, 0, sizeof cf_fr); const char** cf_lp; int cf_ln; CufetFailure cf_fe; if (cufet_file_read_lines({path-c}, &cf_lp, &cf_ln, &cf_fe)) \{ cser_text* cf_ls = cser_text_new(); for (int cf_lj = 0; cf_lj < cf_ln; cf_lj++) cser_text_append(cf_ls, cf_lp[cf_lj]); cf_fr.ok = 1; cf_fr.value = cf_ls; \} else cf_fr.failure = cf_fe; cf_fr; \})".
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The read-c becomes "(\{ cfl_text cf_fr; memset(&cf_fr, 0, sizeof cf_fr); const char* cf_v; CufetFailure cf_fe; if (cufet_file_read_all({path-c}, &cf_v, &cf_fe)) \{ cf_fr.ok = 1; cf_fr.value = cf_v; \} else cf_fr.failure = cf_fe; cf_fr; \})".
            Done.
            Cast one's register-failable on (read-kind).
            Return cast one's c-unwrapped on (read-c, read-kind).
        Done.
        If kind is "FailurePropagate", return cast one's c-pass-off on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        // `<call> but on failure <default>` — the default worked out only when the call failed.
        Define held as cast one's raw-kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define written as cast one's raw-c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-failable on (held) is false, return written.
        Define inner as cast failable-inner on (held).
        Define fallback as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), inner) or pass the failure off.
        Return "(\{ {cast failable-c-name on (held)} cf_r = {written}; cf_r.ok ? cf_r.value : ({fallback}); \})".
    Done.

    /// `the message of`, `the category of` a failure.
    Bind text to failure-field-kind, given (the text field-name):
        If field-name is "message", return "text".
        If field-name is "category", return "voidable text".
        Return "".
    Done.

    Bind text to c-failure-field, given (the text failure-c, the text field-name):
        If field-name is "message", return "({failure-c}).message".
        Return "(\{ CufetFailure cf_f = {failure-c}; cf_f.category ? cvo_text_some(cf_f.category) : cvo_text_none(); \})".
    Done.

    // ── Statements ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `Cast <call> or pass the failure off.`, or a call that can fail made inside a `Try`.
    Bind void or failure to emit-failable-cast unto emitter, given (the node call, the fact passes-off):
        If passes-off:
            Cast one's line on ("{cast one's c-pass-off on (call) or pass the failure off};").
            Return.
        Done.
        Cast one's line on ("{cast one's c-of on (call) or pass the failure off};").
    Done.

    /// `Try to: … In case of failure: …` — a failure inside goes to the handler, which sees it as
    /// `the failure`, and the program goes on after both.
    Bind void or failure to emit-try unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("In case of exception")).
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)), return a failure (cast not-built on ("a Try with no failure handler")).
        Define label as "{(cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word}_{(cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s word}".
        Define outer-try as cast one's current-try.
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Cast one's line on ("CufetFailure cf_failure_{label}; memset(&cf_failure_{label}, 0, sizeof cf_failure_{label});").
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes label.
        Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes outer-try.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
        Cast one's line on ("goto cf_tried_{label};").
        Cast one's line on ("cf_try_{label}: \{").
        // The handler, in the `Try` around this one — and with `the failure` named.
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "the failure" becomes "failure".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%the failure" becomes "failure".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "@the failure" becomes "".
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "        ".
        Cast one's line on ("CufetFailure {cast c-name on ("the failure")} = cf_failure_{label};").
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Cast one's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
        Cast one's line on ("cf_tried_{label}: ;").
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.

    /// What a function that can only fail or be done says when it reaches its end: done.
    Bind void to close-failable unto emitter:
        If (the entry for "%return" in one's kinds but void is "") is "failure of void":
            Cast one's line on ("return cfl_void_done();").
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
